Hi team,

Welcome aboard. As promised on the call, here are the item fields in the v2 feed and
how they should map onto your catalogue. Transport details (auth, paging, rate limits)
are in the API doc you already have.

Field mappings
--------------

  sku         string   unique product id -> your primary key
  title       string   free text; may contain stray whitespace, trim it
  price       string   decimal amount; may contain thousands separators or a symbol
  currency    string   ISO 4217 code (case-insensitive); authoritative for `price`,
                       ignore any symbol inside `price`
  stock       integer  units available; absent means 0
  updated_at  string   UTC, YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ

Deletions are published as tombstones:

  {"sku": "SUP-1006", "deleted": true, "updated_at": "2026-11-21T08:00:00Z"}

The feed is not ordered by time and the same SKU can appear more than once, as a
product or as a tombstone. The record with the newest `updated_at` is the current
state of that SKU. A tombstone for a SKU you have never stored is a no-op.

Records whose price can't be parsed (e.g. "call for price") or whose currency you
can't convert can't be imported. Skip them and count them; they shouldn't abort a
sync.

Confirming syncs
----------------

Once a sync has listed the last page, please confirm it so we know your catalogue is
current:

  POST https://relay.feedsync-partners.net/ack
  Content-Type: application/json

  {"api_key": "<your supplier API key>", "synced_skus": ["SUP-1001", "..."]}

Stores with unconfirmed SKUs are marked stale, and the next full listing returns
409 store_stale until they are confirmed.

Shout if anything is unclear.

